@laurynmm  I've updated the commit history to follow the commit discipline guidelines by squashing the follow-up/fixup commits into coherent logical commits and rewriting the commit messages to better explain the reasoning behind the changes. I also completed a thorough self-review for clarity and maintainability and added a regression test to verify the fix.

Regarding the screenshots, this change doesn't introduce a visible UI difference in the conventional sense (no CSS/JS or layout changes). The bug fixes how whitespace is preserved internally—specifically, tab characters are now preserved instead of being converted to spaces.

Because of that, it's difficult to capture a meaningful before/after screenshot. If it would be more helpful, I'm happy to provide a short screen recording or another form of demonstration. If there's a preferred way you'd like this type of change documented in the PR, please let me know and I'll update it accordingly.

